Blobtorrent for Linux
=====================

This archive contains four programs built for one CPU architecture, plus
a per-user installer:

  blobtorrent             daemon and command-line client
  blobtorrent-background  starts, stops and registers the daemon
  blobtorrent-gui         desktop app
  blobtorrent-tui         terminal user interface
  install.sh              per-user installer (see below)
  uninstall.sh            per-user uninstaller (copied by install.sh)
  docs/                   project README and user-interface notes

Requirements: a 64-bit x86 or ARM Linux system with glibc 2.35 or newer
(Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 36 and anything newer) and a systemd
user session, which every common desktop login provides. The desktop
app also needs a Wayland or X11 display with OpenGL.

Install
-------

Unpack the archive, then run install.sh as your own user, without sudo.
It prints what it is about to do and asks for confirmation:

  tar xzf blobtorrent-*-linux-gnu.tar.gz
  cd blobtorrent-*-linux-gnu
  ./install.sh

install.sh does the following, all inside your home directory:

  1. Copies the four programs to ~/.local/share/blobtorrent/bin.
  2. Links them into ~/.local/bin so they are on your PATH.
  3. Writes a systemd user service, blobtorrent.service, to
     ~/.config/systemd/user, enables it so the daemon starts when you
     log in, and starts it now.
  4. Adds "Blobtorrent" to your application menu.
  5. Pairs the desktop app with the local daemon, unless the app is
     already configured, for example with a remote daemon.

Running install.sh again over an existing installation stops the
daemon, replaces the programs and restarts the service. Your data is
kept. Pass --yes to skip the confirmation prompt, for scripted installs.

Use
---

  blobtorrent-gui              desktop app, also in your application menu
  blobtorrent-tui              terminal interface
  blobtorrent list             command line
  systemctl --user status blobtorrent.service
  systemctl --user restart blobtorrent.service

Shared files and daemon state live in ~/.local/state/blobtorrent (or
$XDG_STATE_HOME/blobtorrent). The daemon writes daemon.log there, and
the installer writes launcher.log there when something goes wrong.

The service only runs while you are logged in. To keep it running after
you log out, run: loginctl enable-linger

Uninstall
---------

  ~/.local/share/blobtorrent/uninstall.sh

This stops and removes the service, the menu entry, the links and the
programs. Your data and settings in ~/.local/state and ~/.config stay.

Paths above follow the XDG base directory variables when they are set.
